; NPC daily routines (read by src/routine.c at boot; "reload routines" rereads it).
;
; Each block starts with #<mob vnum> and gives the timetable of every copy of
; that mobile.  Hours are mud hours, 0-23.  Lines starting with ';' are
; comments, and the file ends with '$'.
;
;   <hour> go <room vnum> [stand|sit|rest|sleep]
;            From this hour on the mobile should be in that room.  It walks
;            there one room per mobile pulse (opening doors on the way), then
;            takes up the position given (default stand).  The latest 'go' at
;            or before the current hour is in force, wrapping round midnight,
;            so a mobile that is killed or reset simply walks to wherever it
;            should be.  A sleeping mobile wakes when its next 'go' comes up.
;   arrive say|emote <text>    said or done on reaching the room of the 'go'
;                              line above it
;   leave say|emote <text>     said or done on setting off from the room of
;                              the 'go' line above it, when the next one starts
;   <hour> say <text>          said on the hour, if awake
;   <hour> emote <text>        "<name> <text>", e.g. "rings the temple bell."
;   idle [<from>-<to>] <pct> say|emote <text>
;            a chance in <pct> percent, each pulse, of one idle line while it
;            is settled somewhere and a player is there to hear it; the
;            optional hour range limits when (it may wrap, e.g. 20-4)
;
; Text may not contain '$'.  A mobile with no 'go' lines stays where it is
; and only talks.  A shopkeeper who leaves his shop, or sleeps in it, puts
; up a CLOSED sign (obj 32), and the shop is shut until he is back and
; awake.  Give routines only to mobiles that exist once in the world: every
; copy of a mobile follows the same timetable.
;
; Weather: in a downpour (pouring rain, a thunderstorm or tornado, a
; snowstorm or blizzard) a mobile whose 'go' room is out of doors stays
; wherever it is indoors, or if it is out in it runs for the nearest indoor
; room in the zone, and goes back to its timetable when the weather eases.
; One indoors won't set off through the open while it pours, unless it is
; going to bed ('sleep').  So give outdoor jobs an indoor room nearby, and
; flag shops and taverns INDOORS in the world files.

